    "chunk_size_bytes": 1425,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cAt Group level, Pink Eagle\u2019s mission is equally focused on strategically investing in highpotential industries, providing strong leadership and governance, and cultivating a culture of innovation, integrity, and performance. Moreover, the Group is able to unlock synergies among the subsidiaries through collaboration and optimized resources, creating longterm, sustainable value and empowering every business unit to excel,\u201d said Silva.\n\nIndika Abeywickrama, Director\u2013Tea, Continental Tea said, \u201cCelebrating a decade of ADRA Ceylon, we take pride in becoming one of Sri Lanka\u2019s top tea exporters. Our journey of quality, innovation, and global expansion has supported communities and contributed to the country\u2019s export earnings. Throughout the years, we have invested in dedicated warehouse infrastructure and advanced blending and packing machinery to boost production capacity and output quality. In parallel, we will continue to invest in value-added tea products and the development of the ADRA brand throughout international markets, positioning it as a premium Ceylon Tea brand for the modern global consumer.\u201d\n\nComplementing the group\u2019s logistics capabilities is Abanchy Ceylon, which provides smart, reliable freight solutions by air, sea, and land. Over the past year, Abanchy has expanded into the East African market, thereby broadening the group\u2019s logistics reach covering three continents."
