    "chunk_size_bytes": 1330,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe believe it is our shared responsibility to elevate Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism industry to the next level,\u201d stated Vella Director and co-founder Eranda Abeyratne, capturing the core vision behind the investment.\n\nThe extensive expansion stands as a testament to the Vella group\u2019s unwavering long-term vision of delivering immersive, experience-led hospitality that remains globally competitive while deeply rooted in Sri Lanka\u2019s extraordinary natural beauty and cultural identity.\n\nThrough this agreement, the Vella group and BOI signal a shared ambition to position the country not merely as a tourist destination but as a standard-bearer for sustainable luxury hospitality across Asia.\n\nThe Vella group operates as a diversified Sri Lankan conglomerate with extensive interests across hospitality, adventure tourism, tea, retail, leisure and lifestyle-led experiences. Its expansive portfolio includes some of Sri Lanka\u2019s most distinctive destinations and brands, featuring 98 Acres Resort & Spa, Walaa Kulu, Villa le Maas Tota, Flying Ravana Adventure Park, Ravana Pool Club, Kiri Kopi Caf\u00e9s, Uva Halpewatte Tea Factory, Halpe Tea Exports and Ceylon Tea Supermarkets.\n\nRooted in experience, innovation and people-led growth, the group continues to create unique experiences bridging Sri Lanka to the rest of the world."
