    "md5": "968fbe06743427666863ee6b096b8f8e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1653,
    "chunk_text": "INFRACON 2026 to shape future of infrastructure development in Sri Lanka\n\nThe Infrastructure and Construction Exhibition (INFRACON 2026), a premier industry event dedicated to the country\u2019s infrastructure and construction sectors, will take place from 3 to 5 July at the Sirimavo Bandaranaike Memorial Exhibition Centre (SBMEC), Colombo.\n\nThe event is organised by Lanka Exhibition and Conference Services Ltd., (LECS) a winner of multiple Presidential Awards in the MICE category and inductee into the MICE Hall of Fame, and Savor International Ltd., from Bangladesh, who is also an industry leader in the MICE sector in Bangladesh.\n\nPreviously known as the \u2018Construction, Power and Energy Expo,\u2019 the exhibition has now been rebranded as \u2018INFRACON 2026,\u2019 and is endorsed and supported by the American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air-Conditioning Engineers Sri Lankan Chapter (ASHRAE) and the Solar Industries Association (SIA), further strengthening its industry relevance.\n\nINFRACON 2026 will bring together industry leaders, policymakers, developers, contractors, engineers, architects, and technology providers, while featuring organisations and suppliers from five major sectors consisting of HVAC-R and Cold Chain, Power and Energy, Green Grid, Safe Water, and Build Materials, which will be showcased within the exhibition as individual concurrent segments, serving as a catalyst for growth and collaboration in Sri Lanka\u2019s rapidly evolving infrastructure landscape, with participation from leading local and international exhibitors, shaping the future of infrastructure development in Sri Lanka and the South Asian region."
  },
