    "chunk_text": "Private bus unions to decide on next move today\n\nColombo, June 2 (Daily Mirror) - Private bus operators are scheduled to meet today (02) to decide on the future course of action regarding the failure to increase bus fares following the recent diesel price hike.\n\nChairman of the Lanka Private Bus Owners\u2019 Association, Gemunu Wijeratne, said a final decision on bus operations would be taken after discussions with representatives of all bus associations.\n\nHe said the meeting is scheduled to take place this morning with participation from representatives of several transport associations.\n\n\u201cOur representatives and other association representatives are coming today. Specifically, we are discussing how to save our industry from the fuel problem. The government is not responding. They are on a certain policy,\u201d Wijeratne said.\n\nHe further warned that private bus owners could unanimously decide to withdraw from operations if a solution is not provided.\n\n\u201cHowever, we as an association will discuss with the leaders and announce the final decision today,\u201d he added."
