    "md5": "75a6d79cdd0b8bcbbf972401040ffcf0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1704,
    "chunk_text": "NCPC launches National Cleaner Production Awards 2026\n\nAlso unveils 4th International Conference on Resource Efficiency and Circular Economy\n\nThe National Cleaner Production Centre (NCPC) Sri Lanka officially launched two of the country\u2019s most significant sustainability initiatives, National Cleaner Production Awards 2026 (NCPA 2026) and Fourth International Conference on Resource Efficiency and Circular Economy, at a special ceremony held in Colombo recently.\n\nThe event brought together the policymakers, industry leaders, sustainability professionals, development partners, academia and representatives from the private sector to reaffirm Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to advancing sustainable industrial development, resource efficiency, cleaner production and circular economy practices.\n\nThe event was graced by Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara as the chief guest.\n\nWelcoming the gathering, NCPC Sri Lanka Chairman Gamini Gunasekera emphasised the growing importance of sustainable production and consumption in today\u2019s increasingly competitive global environment. He highlighted the need for industries to enhance productivity while minimising environmental impacts and strengthening resilience against climate-related challenges.\n\nDuring the event, NCPC Sri Lanka Chief Executive Officer Samantha Kumarasena presented an overview of the upcoming Fourth International Conference on Resource Efficiency and Circular Economy, which will serve as a global platform for knowledge sharing, innovation, policy dialogue and collaboration among experts, industries, researchers and development organisations working towards a circular economy transition."
