    "chunk_size_bytes": 1399,
    "chunk_text": "BOC installs Digital Tills on Kiri Vehera, Kataragama Devalaya premises\n\nBank of Ceylon (BOC) has installed Digital Tills (digital pin kata) on the sacred Kiri Vehera and historic Ruhunu Maha Kataragama Devalaya premises, enabling the devotees to make donations conveniently and securely through QR-based digital payments.\n\nThe initiative is in line with the government\u2019s and Central Bank of Sri Lanka\u2019s digital road map to build up a cashless economy, under which BOC continues to promote safe, convenient and innovative QR payment solutions for everyday transactions.\n\nThe installation on Kataragama Kiri Vehera premises was carried out under the blessings of Kataragama Kiri Vehera Raja Maha Viharaya Chief Incumbent Venerable Kobawaka Dhaminda Thera and the installation at the Ruhunu Maha Kataragama Devalaya was carried out with the consent of Ruhunu Maha Kataragama Devalaya Basnayake Nilame Thilina Madushanka.\n\nThe event was attended by Administrative Officer E.M. Sanath Ekanayake and this initiative was ceremoniously opened to the public by BOC General Manager and Chief Executive Officer Y.A. Jayathilaka along with BOC\u2019s Southern province corporate and executive management and staff members.\n\nThrough this digital payment platform, the devotees visiting Kiri Vehera and Ruhunu Maha Kataragama Devalaya can now make offerings using a modern, secure and convenient payment method."
