    "chunk_text": "The announcement comes ahead of the July 24 expiration of a 10% temporary tariff imposed by the Trump administration on February 20, the day the Supreme Court struck down U.S. President Donald Trump's tariffs under the International \u200bEmergency Economic Powers Act.\n\nIn the forced labor findings, the USTR said it would exempt from the tariffs a number of products including energy, rare earths and certain \u2060other metals, \u200bbeef, coffee, certain fruits and vegetables, pharmaceuticals, organic chemicals and \u200baircraft parts.\n\nThe USTR said it would accept public comments on the proposed tariffs and other remedies through July 6, with a public \u200bhearing scheduled for July 7."
