    "md5": "ddf1a4140528b237d719b4623ff2d9e6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1690,
    "chunk_text": "The results were significant. Within six months, 20 women were promoted, representing a 2.4-fold increase compared to the previous year, while male promotions also doubled, demonstrating that inclusive systems benefit the wider workforce. Managers and participants reported visible improvements in confidence, ownership, strategic thinking and decision making among female professionals.\n\nAccording to Nimali Senevirathne, Group Head of HR and Legal at Eswaran Brothers, \u201cWomen began leading beyond their titles, showing up with increased visibility, voice and conviction.\u201d\n\nCommenting on the programme, Senela Jayasuriya said, \u201cLeadership is not something you learn. It is something you live.\u201d She added that the programme was designed to create a supportive environment for self-reflection, growth and experimentation, enabling participants to challenge limiting beliefs, build confidence and strengthen their leadership capabilities through real workplace experiences.\n\nParticipants widely described the experience as a mindset shift, helping them focus on what they can control, make decisions with greater clarity and contribute more confidently in their roles. Many reported improvements in time management, delegation, collaboration and communication, while also gaining confidence to engage effectively in traditionally male dominated environments.\n\nShe Transforms has become more than a programme. It is helping build a future-ready, purpose-led workforce of decision makers, problem solvers and resilient leaders. Its measurable impact reflects Eswaran Brothers\u2019 commitment to developing leadership opportunities for women while strengthening organizational performance."
