    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "Chinese children: \u2018Wealth of President Xi Jinping\u2019\n\nHealth is the greatest gift, contentment is the greatest wealth, a trusted friend is the best relative,\n\n\u2018Nirvana\u2019 is the greatest bliss \u2013 The Buddha (\u2018Dhammapada\u2019 Verse 204).\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s trusted all weather friend China is the world\u2019s 2nd largest economy. The Chinese civilization is largely influenced by the teachings of the Buddha, Confucius & Taoism. China celebrated the International Children\u2019s day on June 1, 2026. Marking the occasion, Chinese President Xi Jinping has directed officials to focus on the well being of Chinese Children which is the highest priority of China\u2019s national agenda.\n\nBuddhists believe that all diseases are categorized into two main parts as mental diseases & physical diseases according to the vivid nature of their symptoms. Those in societies which prevents such situations shall hence, prosper. As the leader of socialist China which ensures the right to life for more than 20% of global human population, President Xi has always encouraged children to study hard, exercise regularly, & cultivate both strong minds & strong bodies during his visits to schools across the China (Ref. Media).\n\nIn May 1985, as the Communist Party chief of Hebei Province\u2019s Zhengding County, he visited a village in the county to inspect ongoing renovation work of the local primary school. As he was leaving Zhengding for a new post in Xiamen in Fujian Province, he gave his 3 months\u2019 salary to the principal, saying \u2018I shall leave Zhengding tomorrow. Please use this money to buy books for the children.\u2019\n\nIn 2019 while visiting a primary school in the mountainous hinterland of southwest China\u2019s Chongqing, Xi directed villagers to ensure children in impoverished mountainous regions to have access to education & enjoy a joyous childhood.\u2019"
