    "chunk_size_bytes": 1854,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Melwa occupies a most exclusive waterfront land plot overlooking both the marina and Indian Ocean horizon. While many developments may offer views of water, very few are built upon a land plot that enjoys direct marina frontage while maintaining uninterrupted ocean exposure. What gives the project deeper significance, however, is not only its scale. It is the precision behind its positioning. Not all waterfront land plots carry the same value. The difference is determined by frontage, orientation, visibility and proximity to the water. Prime Melwa benefits from all four. This distinction creates something far more valuable than a premium address. It creates scarcity.\n\nThe architectural vision has been developed to maximise the advantages of the marina-front land plot through orientation, natural light, panoramic views and skyline presence. Rather than functioning as a standalone residential tower, the project has been conceived as a landmark destination shaped by its relationship with the waterfront.\n\nThe architectural vision for Prime Melwa is led by P&T Group Singapore, a globally recognised design practice with a heritage dating back to 1868. Renowned for shaping some of Asia\u2019s most prominent urban and waterfront landmarks, P&T\u2019s portfolio spans major international cities and decades of architectural innovation. Their involvement brings a distinguished level of design prestige to a development already defined by one of Colombo\u2019s most exclusive marina-front land plots.\n\nPrime Melwa represents more than another luxury residential project. It reflects the growing importance of location as the defining factor in long-term real estate value. While future developments may introduce new amenities and new concepts, the most desirable land plots remain limited. That is what makes Prime Melwa particularly significant."
