    "language": "en",
    "md5": "125b844d598034ef09e145cb9fa11c99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1686,
    "chunk_text": "Pan Asia Bank wins Gold at Qorus Reinvention Awards APAC 2026\n\nPan Asia Bank Chief Information Officer Kanchana Devasurendra hands over Qorus Reinvention Awards APAC 2026 Gold award to Pan Asia Bank Director and Chief Executive Officer Naleen Edirisinghe\n\nPan Asia Bank has brought home a major international win, securing the Gold award at Qorus Reinvention Awards APAC 2026, ahead of some of the region\u2019s most established banking institutions, including leading regional players such as DBS Singapore.\n\nOrganised by Qorus, the awards recognise the banks that are reshaping the future of financial services through innovation, digital transformation and operational excellence.\n\nPan Asia Bank was recognised in the Operations and Workforce Transformation Category, for its in-house solution FalconEye.\n\nThe internally developed FalconEye was a key initiative by Chief Information Officer Kanchana Devasurendra, aimed at transforming the way work gets done making it simpler, faster and more effective for teams across the bank. Solution integrates data, processes and teams into a single intelligent platform.\n\nIt helps staff make better decisions in real time, reduces manual effort and improves overall efficiency. While it works behind the scenes, the real impact is felt by the customers through faster service and a more seamless banking experience.\n\nThis recognition stands out not just for the award itself but for what it represents: the Truly Sri Lankan bank competing on equal footing with some of the biggest names in global banking and coming out on top. It reflects a mindset that values innovation, adaptability and the ability to solve real problems in practical ways."
  },
