    "md5": "7529c0939925110ef0c166d473762ab9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1957,
    "chunk_text": "Pink Eagle Group Chairman and Managing Director Asitha Silva emphasised, \u201cPink Eagle\u2019s strength lies in combining Sri Lanka\u2019s traditions with a modern, global mindset. At our core, there is a clear vision to build a resilient and future-ready business group that delivers sustainable value, drives innovation, and empowers each subsidiary to achieve exceptional growth and global competitiveness.\u201d\n\nTaking centre stage for the organisation in 2026 are several important milestones. Firstly, the flagship entity of Pink Eagle Holdings, Continental Tea Ltd. and its ADRA Ceylon brand celebrate a decade of excellence. In its 10 years of operation, the company is already recognised as a leading exporter of pure Ceylon Tea, serving markets throughout Asia, Europe, and the Middle East, with plans to enter the local market within 2026. Its supply chain is anchored in sustainability, supporting plantation communities through ethical sourcing and long-term value creation.\n\nContinental Tea Director\u2013Tea Indika Abeywickrama said, \u201cCelebrating a decade of ADRA Ceylon, we take pride in becoming one of Sri Lanka\u2019s top tea exporters. Our journey of quality, innovation, and global expansion has supported communities and contributed to the country\u2019s export earnings. Throughout the years, we have invested in dedicated warehouse infrastructure and advanced blending and packing machinery to boost production capacity and output quality. In parallel, we will continue to invest in value-added tea products and the development of the ADRA brand throughout international markets, positioning it as a premium Ceylon Tea brand for the modern global consumer.\u201d\n\nComplementing the group\u2019s logistics capabilities is Abanchy Ceylon, which provides smart, reliable freight solutions by air, sea, and land. Over the past year, Abanchy has expanded into the East African market, thereby broadening the group\u2019s logistics reach covering three continents."
  },
