    "md5": "facbdee9af4e60084649360d52146126",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 604,
    "chunk_text": "SLITA awards 596 diplomas\n\nIndustries Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara addressed the Diploma and Higher National Diploma Certificate Presentation Ceremony, organised by the Sri Lanka Institute of Textiles and Apparel (SLITA) at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH) yesterday. She said the apparel industry, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading export sector, is expected to contribute US$4.9 billion to the country\u2019s projected export earnings of US$17.25 billion in 2025. A total of 596 graduates received diplomas and higher national diplomas at the ceremony. Pix by Kithsiri De Mel."
  },
