    "md5": "1464957e22257ad1839f6f2c51d3d347",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 611,
    "chunk_text": "Water cut in Rajagiriya, Nawala and Kolonnawa areas\n\nColombo, June 5 (Daily Mirror) - The National Water Supply and Drainage Board (NWSDB) announced that water supply to several areas will be suspended until 8.00 p.m. today due to a sudden rupture in the main water transmission pipeline from Ambatale to Kolonnawa.\n\nThe affected areas are Moragasmulla, Rajagiriya, Nawala, Obeysekara Pura and the Kolonnawa Urban Council area.\n\nThe Board said repair work is underway and expressed regret for the inconvenience caused to consumers.\n\nFurther information can be obtained by contacting the NWSDB's hotline on 1939."
  },
