    "chunk_text": "Although a limited number of LINAC machines are currently available in Sri Lanka's state hospital network, he stressed that the number should be more than doubled to meet growing demand. He also called for the immediate expansion of treatment facilities to reduce waiting times for cancer patients requiring radiation therapy.\n\nHe further pointed out that more than 15,000 cancer-related deaths are reported annually in Sri Lanka, while nearly 1,000 children are newly diagnosed with cancer each year. Annual deaths among paediatric cancer patients exceed 200, underscoring the urgent need to strengthen cancer treatment services in the country, he said."
