    "chunk_text": "Then, just as the ground becomes too hard to absorb water, the rains will return with a vengeance. The Kelani, Gin, and Nilwala rivers will rise faster than our warning systems can react. Urban Colombo, already sinking and clogged, will become a basin.\n\nFrankly, no. Our early warning systems are still manual and slow. Our irrigation canals are 500 years old and leaking. Our food security policy still hinges on a single crop (paddy) that drowns in two hours of rain and dies in two weeks without it.\n\nHowever, \"not ready\" is not the same as \"doomed.\" The next 18 months are the last window to convert this prophecy into a work plan.\n\n1)For Food Security: Stop Farming Like it is 1980s.We cannot afford to gamble an entire Yala season on paddy. The Department of Agriculture must immediately issue a compulsory diversification order for the 2025/26 Maha season.\n\nShort-cycle crops: Shift 30% of paddy land in the Dry Zone to manioc, sweet potato, and green gram crops that survive on fog and dew.\n\nThe Home Garden Army: Every household with a square foot of land must plant jak, breadfruit, and kohila. The government should waive the Agrarian Development Act fees for home garden wells.\n\nStrategic Reserves: We need to fill silos not just with rice, but with seed paddy for drought-resistant varieties (Bg 360, At 362). In 2026, seeds will be worth more than gold.\n\nImmediate: Complete the retrofitting of the Kelanitissa and Sapugaskanda power plants to run on cheaper Liquefied Natural Gas (LNG), not diesel. Every dollar saved on fuel in 2026 is a dollar for medicine.\n\nRadical: The CEB must publish a \"Drought Tariff\" by December 2025. Large water users (plantations, textile dyeing, hotels) must pay a steep sliding scale for water drawn from reservoirs. We must price scarcity before the scarcity prices us.\n\n3.The Aswesuma welfare system is not designed for climate shocks."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-06-05-dailymirrorlk-95542e34",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-95542e34",
    "date_str": "2026-06-05",
    "description": "The Super El Ni\u00f1o is Not a Prophecy of Doom. It is a Deadline.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/breaking-news/The-Super-El-Ni\u00f1o-is-Not-a-Prophecy-of-Doom-It-is-a-Deadline/108-342048",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1780638951.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-06-05-dailymirrorlk-95542e34-0002",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9c22e8c73224c7e6e63a43470f4cc0c2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1650,
    "chunk_text": "Radical: The CEB must publish a \"Drought Tariff\" by December 2025. Large water users (plantations, textile dyeing, hotels) must pay a steep sliding scale for water drawn from reservoirs. We must price scarcity before the scarcity prices us.\n\n3.The Aswesuma welfare system is not designed for climate shocks.\n\nThe Three Day Rule: Every Grama Niladhari division in a flood zone must identify a high ground assembly point and stock it with dry rations and water purification tablets by April 2026. Not a plan. A pallet.\n\nThe greatest obstacle is not our lack of resources, but our love of the \"middle path.\" We wait for the President to make a statement. We wait for the IMF to release funds. We wait for the rain to come.\n\nWe saw in 2022 what happens when we run out of foreign reserves for fuel. In 2026, we will run out of water and food. The same panic, the same lines, the same helplessness unless we treat this as a national security mobilization.\n\nThe farmer in Mahiyangana needs a drought-resistant seed today, not a prayer in 2026. The resident of Modara needs a canal dredged today, not a helicopter rescue in two years.\n\nConsider this not a prophecy of doom, but a rare gift: a natural disaster we can see coming from two years away. No earthquake gives us that warning. No tsunami allows for preparation.\n\nIf we spend 2026 arguing, procrastinating, and politicking, then the end of 2026 will indeed be hell. But if we use this deadline to diversify our crops, harden our power grid, and clean our drainage, we will do something extraordinary to fight against this deadline. This catastrophic climate event does not wait for cabinet approval."
  },
