    "chunk_size_bytes": 1911,
    "chunk_text": "Sangakkara Joins Women Cricketers\u2019 Transformation Meeting\n\nJune.05 (Mirror Sports) - Players of the National Team, Sri Lanka \u2018A\u2019, and Under-19 teams participated in the meeting, which was chaired by Eran Wickramaratne, Chairman of the Cricket Transformation Committee.\n\nOther members of the committee, namely Prakash Schaffter, Honorary Secretary of Sri Lanka Cricket; Sidath Wettimuny, Chairman of the Cricket Committee; Roshan Mahanama; and Kumar Sangakkara, also took part in the meeting.\n\nDinal Phillips, President\u2019s Counsel; Upul Kumarapperuma, President\u2019s Counsel; Avanthi Colombage; and Thushira Raddella, who are also members of the Cricket Transformation Committee, were present alongside Ashley De Silva, CEO of Sri Lanka Cricket, and Jamie Siddons, Head Coach of the Sri Lanka National Women\u2019s Team.\n\nAddressing the women cricketers, Eran Wickramaratne commended the remarkable progress of women\u2019s cricket in Sri Lanka and described the team\u2019s Asia Cup triumph as \u201crewriting the history of women\u2019s cricket in Sri Lanka.\u201d\n\nWhile praising the players for their dedication and hard work, Wickramaratne stated that the Cricket Transformation Committee would work towards ensuring that women\u2019s cricket receives the same level of attention, opportunities, and support afforded to men\u2019s cricket.\n\nHe also conveyed his best wishes to the Sri Lanka National Women\u2019s Team ahead of their participation in the ICC Women\u2019s T20 World Cup 2026.\n\nIn addition, Wickramaratne, Sidath Wettimuny, Kumar Sangakkara, and Roshan Mahanama addressed the players, offering valuable advice on building successful cricketing careers while maintaining a strong focus both on and off the field.\n\nThe cricketing greats emphasized that teamwork is the foundation of success and stressed the importance of every player understanding and fulfilling their role within the team to achieve positive results."
