    "chunk_text": "Seker added, \u201cBitcoin Pizza Day has become one of crypto\u2019s most celebrated traditions because it captures something essential: innovation happens when someone is willing to try something new, even if it seems impractical at the time. In 2010, Laszlo Hanyecz used Bitcoin to buy pizza because he believed digital currency should have use cases, not just sit in a wallet.\n\nBinance continues to expand its educational initiatives across South Asia, reaching millions of learners globally through its Binance Academy platform. The Colombo event is part of Binance\u2019s expanding education initiatives in Sri Lanka, which include ChainCeylon 2026, a flagship university program launched earlier this year.\n\nThe initiative has already engaged 265 students across the University of Sri Jayewardenepura, University of Kelaniya, Wayamba University, and University of Moratuwa through interactive workshops on on-chain analysis, real-world blockchain applications, and foundational digital asset principles."
