    "md5": "54cdc741d52b2c718e27b3684eef998d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1883,
    "chunk_text": "Moshe Safdie\u2019s 240 meter Altair receives PWA\u2019s entrance and lobby upgrade\n\nAltair, an address that elevates and defines contemporary living, stands as MosheSafdie\u2019s architectural masterpiece and a powerful statement that buildings can achieve extraordinary feats. Rising above Colombo\u2019s traditionally horizontal urban fabric of traffic and density, Altair introduced a different architectural grammar: a vision of living beautifully in Colombo through vertical innovation, space, light, and lifestyle.\n\nAltair has recently unveiled a refined upgrade to its entrance and lobby, creating a renewed arrival experience for residents and visitors alike. Executed by Philip Weeraratne Associates (PWA), the enhancements were carefully designed to strengthen Altair\u2019s premium residential identity while respecting the integrity and character of Safdie\u2019s original architectural vision.\n\nAt the entrance, the previous frontage has been transformed into a bold and elegant architectural statement through the introduction of bronze-toned vertical fins, warm ambient lighting, lush greenery, and a central branded feature panel. The fins introduce rhythm, depth, and sophistication, while the integrated lighting creates a distinctive evening presence. Green walls and curated landscaping soften the built form and deliver a welcoming, resort-inspired arrival experience.\n\nThe lobby upgrade reimagines the dramatic triple-height volume as a luxurious residential lounge rather than merely a transitional space. While preserving the openness, natural light, and restrained material palette of the original design, the new concept introduces curated seating clusters, textured rugs, marble tables, indoor planting, and vertical green features. These interventions create intimate pockets within the expansive volume, bringing warmth, comfort, and vibrancy to the interior environment."
  },
