    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "149e566e1ab6bef03a63b3d88fc21648",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1954,
    "chunk_text": "Port City offers strong investment potential, says VIA 9 founder\n\nColombo Port City has significant potential to attract new investments and support emerging businesses, according to entrepreneur Avin Fernando, founder of Italian restaurant VIA 9, one of the latest ventures to establish operations within the country\u2019s offshore business hub.\n\nFernando, who launched VIA 9 in December last year with a group of investors, said the project was born out of his passion for authentic Italian cuisine and confidence in the long-term prospects of Port City Colombo.\n\nBorn and raised in Italy, Fernando said he spent much of his childhood in his father\u2019s restaurant, where he was exposed to the food industry from an early age.\n\n\u201cMy father has managed a restaurant in Italy for nearly 40 years. Growing up, I spent a lot of time there, helping out in the kitchen and learning the trade. That experience inspired my passion for Italian food and motivated me to start something of my own,\u201d he said.\n\nFernando said VIA 9 aims to offer Sri Lankans a more authentic Italian dining experience, noting that many consumers have not had the opportunity to experience traditional Italian dishes prepared according to their original recipes.\n\n\u201cWe import selected ingredients directly from Italy and brought in an Italian team to train our local staff. Our objective is to deliver authentic Italian flavours rather than adapting recipes to resemble fast food,\u201d he said. Looking ahead, Fernando said the restaurant plans to introduce \u201cshow cooking\u201d, where meals are prepared in front of customers, offering a more interactive dining experience.\n\n\u201cWhen people visit a restaurant, they usually don\u2019t see what happens behind the scenes. Show cooking allows guests to watch the preparation process and engage with the experience,\u201d he said.\n\nThe company is also exploring plans to expand beyond Colombo, with a second outlet in Negombo under consideration."
  },
