    "md5": "036091df4b7187cba9577f62211c8eea",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1124,
    "chunk_text": "British Tamils remember Mullivaikkal Day in London\n\nIn memory of those who died, lamps were lit and flowers were laid at a makeshift grave\n\nRemembering those who died at the final stage of Sri Lanka\u2019s ethnic war,\u00a0 Tamils in London\u00a0 organised several events including a protest walk and other events on May 18 2026.\n\nMarking the 17 years since the end of war in Mullivaikkal in 2009, a rally began at Parliament Square, the place where the Tamil community staged weeks-long protests in 2009, urging the international community to intervene in\u00a0 Sri Lanka\u2019s civil war.\n\nThe protesters held flags as they marched through Westminster and ended outside 10 Downing Street.\u00a0 A memorial for the victims of\u00a0 war was held outside 10 Downing Street. Kalaiyarasi Maniarasan, the Deputy Director of the Tamil Youth Organisation UK (TYO UK) raised the United Kingdom flag.\n\nIn memory of those who died, lamps were lit and flowers were laid at a makeshift grave. This was followed by serving of Mullivaikkal Kanji (symbolic rice offering),\u00a0 remembering the hardships undergone by the Tamil community during the final stage of war."
