    "chunk_text": "Free vehicle tuning dansala on June 10-11\n\nColombo, June 6 (Daily Mirror) - The Department of Motor Traffic (DMT) has announced that a special \u201cvehicle tuning Dansala\u201d will be held on June 10 and 11 in front of its head office in Narahenpita.\n\nIn a notice, the DMT said that motorcycles and three-wheelers, which make up the majority of Sri Lanka\u2019s vehicle fleet, often do not receive proper maintenance due to economic difficulties, resulting in increased harmful emissions.\n\nThe programme, organized for the third consecutive time by the DMT\u2019s Motor Vehicle Emissions Trust Fund, aims to improve vehicle performance while reducing environmental pollution.\n\nUnder the initiative, owners of motorcycles and three-wheelers will be able to obtain free vehicle tuning services from some of the country\u2019s most experienced technicians.\n\nThe DMT said the programme is expected to enhance fuel efficiency, reduce unnecessary fuel costs for vehicle owners, and help minimize harmful emissions released into the environment."
