    "chunk_size_bytes": 1751,
    "chunk_text": "Western Province DS offices recognised for President\u2019s fund drive\n\nColombo, June 7 (Daily Mirror) - Divisional Secretariat offices that recorded the highest level of performance under the President\u2019s Fund decentralisation programme in 2025 were honoured at a special recognition ceremony held yesterday (06) at the Miloda Auditorium in Colombo.\n\nThe event was held under the patronage of Speaker and Member of the President\u2019s Fund Board of Governors, Jagath Wickramaratne, to acknowledge the contribution of Divisional Secretariat offices in bringing the services of the President\u2019s Fund closer to the public.\n\nUnder the programme, the Homagama, Kaduwela and Kesbewa Divisional Secretariats in the Colombo District were recognised for their achievements.\n\nIn the Gampaha District, the Gampaha, Biyagama and Mahara Divisional Secretariats received recognition, while the Panadura, Beruwala and Bandaragama Divisional Secretariats were honoured in the Kalutara District.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Secretary to the President\u2019s Fund and Senior Additional Secretary to the President, Roshan Gamage, said the Government\u2019s decision to decentralise the President\u2019s Fund had transformed it from a Colombo-centred institution into a people-oriented service accessible at the grassroots level.\n\nHe said that Divisional Secretariat offices had become the public face of the President\u2019s Fund and played a key role in delivering assistance to vulnerable communities without requiring them to travel to Colombo.\n\nMr. Gamage also commended Divisional Secretaries, Assistant Divisional Secretaries, Accountants, Subject Officers, Grama Niladharis and other field officers for their commitment in implementing the programme despite numerous challenges."
