    "chunk_size_bytes": 1904,
    "chunk_text": "Continental Cars launches Volkswagen Taigun and Virtus in Sri Lanka\n\nNew era of German engineering, innovation and premium mobility begins in Sri Lanka\n\nContinental Cars & Commercials (Pvt.) Ltd, the official authorised importer for Volkswagen passenger vehicles in Sri Lanka, ceremonially launched the all-new Volkswagen Taigun and Virtus, at the prestigious Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall recently.\n\nThe highly anticipated launch marks a historic milestone for Volkswagen in Sri Lanka, reinforcing the brand\u2019s long-term commitment to the local market while introducing a new generation of premium German-engineered mobility solutions designed specifically for modern Sri Lankan consumers.\n\nThe prestigious event brought together senior representatives from the Volkswagen group, diplomats, government officials, corporate leaders, members of the business community, media representatives, industry stakeholders and automotive enthusiasts for an evening celebrating Volkswagen\u2019s global heritage, innovation and future vision for mobility in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe launch event featured an immersive unveiling experience combining advanced digital presentations, cultural performances, entertainment segments, executive presentations and dynamic product showcases that highlighted Volkswagen\u2019s globally recognised standards in engineering, technology, safety and design excellence.\n\nThe launch was conducted in collaboration with Skoda Auto Volkswagen India (Pvt.) Ltd, the regional operational and manufacturing hub for the Volkswagen group brands in India. Skoda Auto Volkswagen India oversees the Indian operations of globally renowned automotive brands including Volkswagen, \u0160koda, Audi, Porsche, Lamborghini and Bentley, while driving innovation, localisation, advanced engineering, manufacturing excellence and customer-focused mobility solutions across the South Asian region."
