    "md5": "3b9588cadb63c24d44db1f1f3d61c43b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1854,
    "chunk_text": "The launch was conducted in collaboration with Skoda Auto Volkswagen India (Pvt.) Ltd, the regional operational and manufacturing hub for the Volkswagen group brands in India. Skoda Auto Volkswagen India oversees the Indian operations of globally renowned automotive brands including Volkswagen, \u0160koda, Audi, Porsche, Lamborghini and Bentley, while driving innovation, localisation, advanced engineering, manufacturing excellence and customer-focused mobility solutions across the South Asian region.\n\nThe all-new Volkswagen Taigun enters the Sri Lankan market as a bold and progressive SUV developed for customers seeking versatility, performance, advanced technology and premium comfort. Built on Volkswagen\u2019s internationally acclaimed engineering platform, Taigun combines sporty styling with intelligent innovation, offering a confident and engaging driving experience for both urban and long-distance travel.\n\nThe all-new Volkswagen Virtus redefines premium sedan mobility with its combination of elegant styling, refined comfort, advanced technology and exhilarating performance. Designed to deliver an elevated driving experience, Virtus combines sophisticated aesthetics with Volkswagen\u2019s signature German engineering standards, offering customers a sedan that balances luxury, practicality, innovation and performance.\n\nSkoda Auto Volkswagen India MD and CEO Piyush Arora stated, \u201cThe introduction of Taigun and Virtus in Sri Lanka marks an important milestone in Volkswagen\u2019s regional growth journey.\u201d\n\nContinental Cars & Commercials Chairman Heinz Reuter stated, \u201cThrough the launch of Taigun and Virtus, we are committed to delivering an exceptional ownership experience supported by premium after-sales service, genuine spare parts, internationally trained technical expertise and modern facilities built to global standards.\u201d"
