    "chunk_size_bytes": 1700,
    "chunk_text": "INFRACON 2026 infrastructure and construction expo in July\n\nINFRACON 2026, Sri Lanka\u2019s first B2B platform for the infrastructure and construction industry, dedicated to South Asia\u2019s infrastructure and construction sectors, will take place from July 3-5, 2026, at the BMICH Colombo.\n\nOrganised by Lanka Exhibitions and Conference Services (Pvt.) Ltd and SAVOR International Limited from Bangladesh, which is also an industry leader in the MICE sector in Bangladesh, INFRACON 2026 is endorsed and supported by the American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air-Conditioning Engineers Sri Lankan Chapter and Solar Industries Association.\n\nINFRACON 2026 will bring together industry leaders, policymakers, developers, contractors, engineers, architects and technology providers, while featuring organisations and suppliers from five major sectors consisting of HVAC-R and cold chain, power and energy, green grid, safe water and build materials, which will be showcased within the exhibition as individual concurrent segments, serving as a catalyst for growth and collaboration in Sri Lanka\u2019s rapidly evolving infrastructure landscape, with participation from leading local and international exhibitors, shaping the future of infrastructure development in Sri Lanka and the South Asian region.\n\nWith international participation from China, India, Pakistan and Bangladesh, SAVOR International will elevate the event to a regional level, highlighting Sri Lanka as a growing hub for the MICE industry in the region, while Sri Lanka\u2019s geographical location and growing hospitality sector makes her the meeting place of choice for industries such as infrastructure and construction to do business."
  },
