    "chunk_text": "Future finance leaders take oath at ACCA Sri Lanka New Member Ceremony 2026\n\nThe FCCA members recognized for their professional excellence and contributions to the profession\n\nACCA Sri Lanka marked a significant milestone in its professional calendar with the hosting of the New Member Ceremony 2026, at Cinnamon Life, Colombo.\n\nThe event brought together newly qualified members, senior professionals, and distinguished guests to celebrate achievement, commitment, and the beginning of a new professional journey within the ACCA global network.\n\nThe ceremony commenced with a welcome address by Dr. Prasenna Balachandran, Chairman of the Member Network Panel (MNP), who set the tone for the evening by reflecting on the values of discipline, integrity, and continuous professional growth that define the ACCA qualification.\n\nA virtual address by Melani Proffit ACCA Global President, followed, adding an international dimension to the programme and reinforcing ACCA\u2019s global reach and connectivity. The evening also featured an inspiring address by Chief Guest, ACCA member from Malaysia, Sim Siew Shan, Group CFO Dialog Axiata PLC who shared her professional journey and experiences, offering valuable insights to the newly inducted members.\n\nRecognising excellence within the community, Mahesh Semage was named ACCA Advocate of the Year 2025, while Lahiru Karunarathna received a Special Recognition award. The Public Sector Advocate of the Year 2025 was awarded to Uresha Walpitagama, acknowledging impactful contributions within the public sector space.\n\nA thought-provoking address titled \u201cRooted in Values, Strengthened by Discipline\u201d was delivered by Suren Rajakarier, Country Managing Partner KPMG Sri Lanka, highlighting the importance of ethical grounding and professional discipline in building sustainable careers."
