    "md5": "9e0de2d467efa0766d57ba6ee161d1f5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1967,
    "chunk_text": "Sampath Bank opens Colombo Port City Branch to advance Sri Lanka\u2019s global investment ambition\n\nFrom left: Ajantha de Vas Gunasekara, Executive Director / Chief Financial Officer; Rushanka Silva, Deputy Chairman; Aroshi Nanayakkara, Independent Non-Executive Director; and Sanjaya Gunawardana, Managing Director/Chief Executive Officer of Sampath Bank PLC, officially opening the Colombo Port City Branch\n\nSampath Bank PLC marked a significant milestone in its growth journey with the official opening of its Colombo Port City Branch, reinforcing its commitment to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s emergence as a globally connected financial and investment destination.\n\nThe opening ceremony was attended by the Sampath Bank Board of Directors, Corporate Management, representatives of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission (CPCEC), Directors from CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt) Ltd, customers, and other distinguished guests.\n\nThe opening of Sampath Bank\u2019s Colombo Port City Branch also marked the first-ever banking transaction within the development, representing another milestone in the evolution of Sri Lanka\u2019s emerging international financial hub.\n\nLocated at Building 1 of the Business Centre, Commercial Hub, Port City Colombo, the branch strengthens Sampath Bank\u2019s presence within Sri Lanka\u2019s first multi-services Special Economic Zone and positions the Bank among the first financial institutions to establish a branch within the development.\n\nThe opening builds on Sampath Bank\u2019s early operational presence following the deployment of a Cash Recycler Machine (CRM) at The Mall at Port City Colombo in 2025, which established the zone\u2019s first banking access points for withdrawal and deposit services.\n\nCustomers also benefit from integrated self-service banking facilities at the newly opened branch, including CRM services, enabling convenient cash withdrawals, deposits, and day-to-day banking transactions within the Port City Colombo ecosystem."
