    "chunk_text": "The patterns observed in complaints from 2023 to 2025 reflect the changing needs of users and new dangers in the Sri Lankan financial system. It is noteworthy to mention that these patterns are also broadly aligned with global trends highlighted in the Consumer Finance Risk Monitor 2026 published by the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD).\n\n(The authors are Assistant Directors at the CBSL Financial Consumer Relations Department)\n\n1.Consumer Finance Risk Monitor 2026 published by Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development\n\n2.Financial Consumer Protection Regulations No. 01 of 2023 of Financial Consumer Relations Department of Central Bank of\n\nThe study of grievances will remain a vital instrument for setting oversight goals and encouraging process improvements for banking sector. By proactively fixing recurring issues, financial firms can improve their behaviour standards, minimise disagreements, and foster greater confidence in the financial system"
