    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e357a1bd504c91ff2cc73316fef423de",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1882,
    "chunk_text": "Peterson Solutions Sri Lanka opens new corporate office at Orion City\n\n\u200bEmbassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in Sri Lanka Deputy Head of Mission / Charg\u00e9 d\u2019Affaires a.i. Iwan Rutjens cuts the ribbon to inaugurate the new Peterson Solutions corporate office at Orion City. Looking on is Peterson Solutions - Asia Pacific Regional Manager Dr. Rukshan Gunatilaka\n\nPeterson Solutions Sri Lanka officially opens its new corporate office at Orion City, Colombo, on 5 June 2026, marking an important milestone in the company\u2019s growth journey and long-term commitment to supporting businesses across Sri Lanka and the wider region.\n\nThe opening ceremony was attended by distinguished guests from the diplomatic and development community, including Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in Sri Lanka Deputy Head of Mission / Charg\u00e9 d\u2019Affaires a.i. Iwan Rutjens, who officiated the ribbon-cutting ceremony. The event also brought together representatives from the European Union, development organisations including the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) and Market Development Facility (MDF) Australia, industry partners, clients and other key stakeholders.\n\nPeterson Solutions is the consultancy and advisory arm of the globally recognised Peterson and Control Union Group, a multinational organization with roots dating back to 1920. Over the past century, the group has grown into a trusted international partner, operating in more than 80 countries, undertaking projects in over 120 countries, and serving a global client base of more than 40,000 through a network of over 6,500 professionals.\n\nBuilt on a legacy of integrity, technical expertise and practical business solutions, Peterson Solutions supports organizations in navigating increasingly complex sustainability, compliance, sourcing, certification and technology-related challenges."
  },
