    "chunk_size_bytes": 1994,
    "chunk_text": "Built on a legacy of integrity, technical expertise and practical business solutions, Peterson Solutions supports organizations in navigating increasingly complex sustainability, compliance, sourcing, certification and technology-related challenges.\n\nThese services help organisations strengthen compliance, improve operational performance, enhance sustainability outcomes, manage risk and create long-term business value.\n\nPeterson Solutions serves a broad range of industries including agriculture, food and beverage, textiles, fisheries, tourism, manufacturing, retail, information technology, logistics, and export-oriented sectors. Its multidisciplinary approach allows businesses to access technical expertise, sustainability knowledge, digital innovation and assurance services through a single integrated platform.\n\nAcross the Asia-Pacific region, Peterson Solutions currently operates through a network of 14 offices, covering Sri Lanka, India, Vietnam, Thailand, Malaysia, Indonesia, Japan, South Korea, China, Taiwan, Papua New Guinea, Pakistan, Australia, and Singapore. This regional footprint enables the organisation to combine local market understanding with international expertise and best practices.\n\nIn Sri Lanka, Peterson Solutions commenced operations in 2023, initially operating from its office in Colombo 03. In just a few years, the company has established itself as a trusted partner to more than 170 clients across Sri Lanka while also supporting projects in the Maldives, Cambodia, and Myanmar.\n\nThe move to Orion City reflects the company\u2019s continued growth, expansion of its consulting team and the increasing demand for value-added services across the region. In addition to its established sustainability and certification offerings, Peterson Solutions has further expanded its capabilities in areas such as crop consultancy, sustainable agriculture, digital solutions, data-driven sustainability management and professional training and capacity development."
  },
