    "chunk_text": "LIVE: Sri Lanka A vs India A, 1st Match at Dambulla\n\nSri Lanka's chase of 278 got off to a positive start as openers Niroshan Dickwella and Avishka Fernando walked out to the middle.\n\nDickwella got the innings underway in style, guiding the first ball from Anshul Kamboj to the fine-leg boundary before rotating the strike, while Avishka also opened his account with a single.\n\nAt the innings break in the first unofficial ODI between Sri Lanka A and India A in Dambulla, India A posted a competitive 277/6 in their 50 overs after being sent in to bat.\n\nDespite an early setback with teenage opener Vaibhav Sooryavanshi dismissed for 14 off 12 balls, India rebuilt their innings through a composed century from captain Ruturaj Gaikwad.\n\nGaikwad anchored the innings with a fluent 101 off 114 deliveries, striking six fours and three sixes, while the middle order provided valuable support to propel India close to the 280-run mark. For Sri Lanka A, Mohamed Shiraz was the standout bowler, claiming 2 wickets for 67 runs from his 9 overs."
