    "md5": "20af0765dc6cfb376328a882acefb18b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 885,
    "chunk_text": "Train services likely to be disrupted amid planned trade union action\n\nColombo, June 9 (Daily Mirror) - Railway services are expected to face major disruption tomorrow due to planned trade union action by railway controllers, the Sri Lanka Railway Controllers\u2019 Union (SLRCU) said.\n\nAssociation Secretary Rukmal Bandara, said that night trains will be operated to complete their journeys. However, he noted that all trains scheduled to begin morning services will not report for duty.\n\nHe warned that the action will significantly affect normal railway operations across the country.\n\nBandara also urged the Sri Lanka Railway Station Masters\u2019 Union (SLRSMU) not to support what he described as \u201cillegal methods\u201d in train operations during the trade union action period.\n\nAuthorities are expected to announce further updates on service adjustments and possible contingency plans."
  },
