    "chunk_text": "In my opinion, this complete bottleneck can be overcome with a very simple solution. For all vendors who already use a card machine, send them their printed QR codes without requiring them to fill in all the documents again. Yes, banks can simply post the QR codes to them. They can send a set with multiple options: one to be kept on a table, a few as stickers, and so on. Vendors will immediately push for QR payments because they do not lose 3%. Rest assured, vendors will even start telling customers, \u201cThis is the cash price,\u201d \u201cThis is the QR price,\u201d and \u201cThis is the card price.\u201d\n\nThe success of QR payments would generate significant savings for the Sri Lankan economy and provide a major boost to the banking system, tourism, trade, and related sectors. Simply posting QR codes to existing credit card machine holders would provide the much-needed kick-start the system requires. The infrastructure has been ready for years; it is the intent that has been lagging behind.\n\n(The author is a resident and guest house owner in Meepilimana, Nuwara Eliya, and can be reached via [email\u00a0protected])"
