    "chunk_size_bytes": 1182,
    "chunk_text": "Indian Naval Ship Sharda calls on Colombo today\n\nIndian Naval Ship Sharda, a Sukanya-class Offshore Patrol Vessel (OPV), will visit Colombo from 10 to 13 June 2026 for an Operational Turnaround (OTR) and the transshipment of stores from the Indian Army for the Sri Lanka Army\u2019s deployment in UN missions. The items will be formally handed over at a ceremony at the Defence Ministry on 16 June 2026.\n\nUpon arrival, the Commanding Officer of the ship, Commander Kartik Sachdeva, will call on the Commander of the Western Naval Area, Rear Admiral SJ Kumara. The ship\u2019s crew will also engage in professional and sporting interactions with the Sri Lanka Navy.\n\nIn the lead-up to the International Day of Yoga, a joint yoga session is being planned for the ship\u2019s crew and Sri Lanka Navy personnel to showcase its benefits in achieving physical, mental, and spiritual well-being.\n\nVisits by Indian Navy vessels to Sri Lanka aim to further strengthen the strong bonds between the two friendly navies, in line with India\u2019s \u2018Neighbourhood First\u2019 policy and the Prime Minister\u2019s vision of \u2018Mutual and Holistic Advancement for Security and Growth Across Regions\u2019 (MAHASAGAR)."
