    "md5": "6fb56c04b60241bedfa28fb4faa1b140",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 812,
    "chunk_text": "Man arrested with forged documents in Kotikawatta\n\nColombo, June 10 (Daily Mirror) - An individual was arrested with a vast range of forged documents during a raid condcuted by the Nugegoda Division Crimes Investigation Unit on a house at Maha Buthgamuwa in Kotikawatta.\n\nPolice carried out the raid on intelligence information received from the Army Intelligence Service.\n\nThe 43-year old suspect is a resident of the Gothatuwa area.\n\nThe forged documents seized by the police included birth certificates, school leaving certificates, business registration certificates, GCE O/L and A/L certificates, degree certificates, JP certificates, Grama Nildhari certificates, medical certificates, vocational training certificates etc.\n\nInvestigations revealed that he had charged about Rs.10,000 for a forged document."
  },
  {
