    "chunk_text": "Home remedies for tired eyes \u2026\n\nI guess all of us are experiencing it \u2026 yes, tired eyes, and I continue to get readers asking me for suggestions.\n\nI\u2019ve touched on this subject before, tired eyes, but I need to oblige my readers \u2026 again, and again!\n\nPop 02 metal spoons in the fridge for 15 minutes. Press the curved side gently on closed eyelids. The cold constricts blood vessels and de-puff and soothes strain.\n\nChill thick cucumber slices (rounds) and then lie down 10 minutes with them on your eyes. Cucumber is 96% water and has antioxidants. It hydrates, cools, and reduces dark circles.\n\nUse cooled green tea bags. Keep cooled green tea bags for 10-15 minutes on closed eyes. First squeeze the excess water, so it doesn\u2019t drip.\n\nWhole milk has lactic acid and fats that soothe and moisturise. Dip cotton pads in chilled milk, press on eyes for 07-10 minutes. Great for those with dry, irritated eyes from screen time.\n\nUse pure aloe vera gel, straight from the plant, chilled. Dab a tiny amount around the orbital bone, not on lids. It cools, hydrates, and the vitamins help with dark circles. Patch test first for sensitive skin.\n\nRaw potato has natural bleaching enzymes and is anti-inflammatory. Keep thin chilled slices, on closed eyes, for 10 minutes. Helps with puffiness and dark circles.\n\nRose water is a natural astringent and smells amazing. Soak cotton pads, chill them, then rest them on eyes for 10 minutes. Refreshes and reduces redness after long hours at the laptop.\n\nNo rubbing eyes, and remember the 20-20-20 rule; every 20 minutes of screen time, look 20 feet away for 20 seconds.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
