    "chunk_text": "\u201cAI tools can be useful at handling volume, but they cannot reliably measure the things that determine whether someone will thrive in a technical team,\u201d said Az Da Rosa, Co-Founder and CEO of Meridian Talent. \u201cIn my experience, the hires that fail are rarely just a skills problem. They\u2019re an alignment problem: working style, communication under pressure, delivery mindset, and cultural fit. Our job is to surface that early, so hiring feels less like a gamble and more like a partnership.\u201d\n\nMeridian Talent\u2019s approach is built on three core principles: real specialist understanding of roles and team context; chemistry and culture fit alongside capability; and a respect-driven process that treats candidates as partners. Rather than relying solely on job descriptions, the firm spends time understanding how a business actually functions: delivery pressures, team dynamics, role expectations, and future direction.\n\nAditya Narayan and Sanka Dineth unite for landmark Sri Lanka\u2013Japan musical collaboration tour\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
