    "chunk_size_bytes": 2015,
    "chunk_text": "Assetline Finance \u2013 preferred partner at David Pieris Automobiles first GWM Flagship Experience Centre\n\nAssetline Finance PLC (AFIN), a member of the David Pieris Holdings, is pleased to be the preferred finance partner for the launch of Sri Lanka\u2019s first GWM Flagship Experience Centre at Access Towers, Colombo by David Pieris Automobiles (Pvt) Ltd (DPA).\n\nThis state\u2011of\u2011the\u2011art facility marks a significant milestone in the country\u2019s evolving automotive retail landscape. As the first and only vehicle experience centre of its kind, it redefines the traditional showroom concept by offering customers an immersive and interactive journey into modern mobility.\n\nVisitors to the centre will be able to explore GWM\u2019s premium range of SUVs, electric vehicles and Plug-in Hybrids (PHV) in a dynamic, experience\u2011led environment. Dedicated display and demonstration zones, interactive touchpoints, and test\u2011drive facilitation will allow customers to engage directly with GWM\u2019s innovation, performance, and design excellence.\n\nAs the preferred finance partner, AFIN promises a seamless finance and ownership process for customers visiting the GWM centre. With super\u2011fast approvals, flexible financing plans, and nationwide support, AFL brings financial convenience directly into the experience centre, making vehicle ownership more accessible and efficient.\n\n\u201cAs the Group\u2019s preferred finance partner, AFIN is delighted to support this flagship launch. Our focus is to simplify the customer journey by offering flexible financing solutions, timely support, and a service experience that helps customers make confident decisions,\u201d said Ashan Nissanka, Director / CEO of AFIN.\n\nThis commitment highlights the strength of integrated service models within David Pieris Holdings. By combining product access with financial expertise, AFIN contributes to a more connected and efficient customer journey, one that reflects Sri Lanka\u2019s growing demand for smarter, future\u2011ready mobility solutions."
