    "chunk_size_bytes": 1521,
    "chunk_text": "CBSL Governor briefs MPs on monetary policy, exchange rate developments\n\nMembers of Parliament yesterday received a briefing on Sri Lanka\u2019s current monetary policy framework, exchange rate developments and broader economic conditions from the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL), as policymakers sought to enhance legislators\u2019 understanding of the country\u2019s ongoing economic recovery efforts.\n\nThe briefing programme, held in Parliament under the patronage of Speaker Dr. Jagath Wickramaratne, was led by CBSL Governor Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe together with a team of senior Central Bank officials.\n\nAccording to a Parliament statement, the session focused on the country\u2019s current monetary policy stance, exchange rate behaviour, economic stability and recent developments relating to Sri Lanka\u2019s economic progress.\n\nCentral Bank officials also engaged with lawmakers during the program, responding to questions and observations raised by Members of Parliament and providing further clarifications on monetary and exchange rate policies.\n\nThe event was attended by Deputy Chairperson of Committees Hemali Weerasekara, Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa, Members of Parliament, Secretary-General of Parliament Kushani Rohanadeera and other parliamentary officials.\n\nThe briefing comes amid heightened public and market interest in monetary policy and exchange rate movements, with the CBSL continuing efforts to maintain macroeconomic stability while supporting the country\u2019s economic recovery and reform agenda."
  },
