    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan rupee edges lower against USD\n\nColombo, June 11 (Daily Mirror) - The Sri Lankan Rupee depreciated slightly against the US Dollar today (11) compared to Wednesday, with both buying and selling rates showing a marginal increase, according to the Central Bank of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe US Dollar selling rate rose to Rs. 337.82, up from Rs. 335.39, while the buying rate increased from Rs. 324.66 to Rs. 327.67.\n\nThe rupee also recorded a slight depreciation against a basket of other major foreign currencies, including the Australian and Canadian Dollars, the Euro, the British Pound Sterling and the Swiss Franc.\n\nWhy Are Fuel Prices Rising in Sri Lanka? The 2026 Crisis Explained"
