    "chunk_text": "SLPP\u2019s Cassilingam urges for better Jaffna train timings to improve connectivity\n\nColombo, June 11 (Daily Mirror) - While welcoming the resumption of the long-awaited Colombo\u2013Jaffna train services, Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) Jaffna District Organizer Geethanath Cassilingam has urged authorities to address concerns over inconvenient train schedules and difficulties faced by the public in obtaining tickets.\n\nDescribing the restored rail service as a vital transport link connecting the North and South, Cassilingam extended his congratulations to both the Sri Lankan and Indian governments for reviving the project.\n\n\u201cI am glad to see the resumption of the much-awaited Colombo\u2013Jaffna train services, which serve as a vital transport route for citizens in the North and South. My heartiest congratulations to the Sri Lankan and Indian governments for resuming this important project,\u201d he said.\n\nHowever, Cassilingam noted that many passengers travelling to and from Jaffna have found the current train schedules inconvenient and called on authorities to review the timings to better suit the needs of commuters.\n\nHe further pointed out that despite train travel being one of the most affordable and preferred modes of transport to the Northern Province, obtaining tickets remains a major challenge for ordinary passengers.\n\nAccording to Cassilingam, a significant number of seats are allocated in advance through government servant warrant reservations, leaving limited opportunities for the general public to secure tickets.\n\nHe urged the government and Transport Minister Bimal Rathnayake to look into the issue and introduce more convenient travel schedules while ensuring fairer access to tickets.\n\nCassilingam also highlighted a strong public demand for a morning train departing from Jaffna, enabling passengers to travel to Colombo, attend to official or personal matters, and return home on the same day."
