    "chunk_text": "MRIA investment project EOI deadline extended until July 9\n\nColombo, June 11 (Daily Mirror) - The deadline for submitting Expressions of Interest (EOIs) for the \u201cProject of Investments to Utilize Resources of Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport (MRIA)\u201d has been extended until July 9, 2026, offering prospective investors additional time to participate in one of Sri Lanka\u2019s key aviation development initiatives.\n\nThe Ports and Civil Aviation Ministry, on behalf of Airport & Aviation Services (Sri Lanka) (Private) Limited (AASL), is seeking proposals from local and international companies, corporations, firms and joint ventures for investments aimed at maximizing the potential of MRIA in Hambantota.\n\nThe project, identified as EOI No. 045/T/2026, covers two major segments: Airside/Aerodrome Operations, which include civil airport activities within the inner perimeter, and Landside Operations, covering activities within both the inner and outer perimeter areas of the airport.\n\nAuthorities said the initiative is intended to attract strategic investors capable of transforming MRIA into a future-ready aviation and investment hub, enhancing global connectivity, promoting sustainable economic growth and creating long-term economic value for Sri Lanka.\n\nA Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee (CANC) has been entrusted with inviting, receiving and evaluating EOIs and selecting eligible parties to proceed to the Request for Proposals (RFP) stage. All communications and submissions relating to the process will be handled through the CANC.\n\nThe EOI process is open to both domestic and international entities. Investors are required to demonstrate their qualifications and relevant experience in carrying out the proposed investments. Shortlisted proponents will be invited to participate in the next stage of the selection process."
