    "md5": "8f276a0baf5bd921687471ad641b64f1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1625,
    "chunk_text": "CameraLK brings global spotlight to Sri Lanka with historic Sony Regional Wildlife Kando at Yala\n\nCameraLK, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading camera retail giant and authorized distributor for Sony in Sri Lanka, hosted the Sony Regional Wildlife Kando at Yala, bringing together some of Asia\u2019s most passionate wildlife photographers and visual storytellers for an unforgettable four-day creative experience in the heart of Sri Lanka\u2019s wilderness.\n\nHeld at the iconic Yala National Park, the event welcomed creators from across the region, including Sri Lanka, Cambodia, Bangladesh, Mongolia, and Myanmar. The gathering marked a significant milestone for Sri Lanka\u2019s photography industry, positioning the island as a key destination for international imaging and wildlife storytelling events.\n\nThe Sony Regional Wildlife Kando was designed to immerse participants in the raw beauty of the natural world while providing unique opportunities to learn, create, and collaborate. Against the breathtaking backdrop of Yala\u2019s diverse landscapes and wildlife, attendees embarked on a series of wildlife safaris, photography expeditions, masterclasses, and hands-on experiences led by industry experts and Sony Alpha Key Opinion Leaders (KOLs).\n\nThroughout the four-day programme, participants ventured deep into the wilderness, capturing remarkable encounters with Sri Lanka\u2019s iconic wildlife, including elusive leopards and majestic elephants. The experience challenged photographers to push the boundaries of their creativity and technical skills while embracing the unpredictability and excitement of real-world wildlife photography."
