    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Throughout the four-day programme, participants ventured deep into the wilderness, capturing remarkable encounters with Sri Lanka\u2019s iconic wildlife, including elusive leopards and majestic elephants. The experience challenged photographers to push the boundaries of their creativity and technical skills while embracing the unpredictability and excitement of real-world wildlife photography.\n\nAdding further significance to the event, the Sony Regional Wildlife Kando at Yala also served as the launch platform for the all-new Sony Alpha a7R VI and FE 100-400mm F4.5 GM OSS lens. Participants were among the first in the region to experience the latest innovations from Sony, testing the new equipment in one of the world\u2019s most demanding and rewarding wildlife photography environments.\n\nCommenting on the event, Anushka Gunasinghe, Managing Director of CameraLK, said, \u201cHosting the Sony Regional Wildlife Kando in Sri Lanka is a proud achievement not only for CameraLK but for the entire local photography community. Bringing together talented creators from across Asia in the stunning landscapes of Yala demonstrates Sri Lanka\u2019s growing prominence on the global photography map. We are honoured to partner with Sony in creating opportunities that inspire creativity, foster learning, and showcase the incredible natural beauty of our country to the world.\u201d\n\nFounded in 2010, CameraLK has rapidly grown to become South Asia\u2019s largest camera retail and online store. Celebrated for its knowledgeable imaging experts, outstanding customer service, and competitive pricing, CameraLK carries over 5,000 products from major manufacturers, including Sony. With branches in Colombo, Kandy, Jaffna, and Batticaloa.\n\nMastercard announces leadership changes to accelerate growth across five key markets in South Asia\n\nLAUGFS Supermarkets partners with Bing Chun to introduce a new lifestyle experience at Pepiliyana outlet"
