    "chunk_text": "Celeste announces leadership appointment\n\nSteps into its next era with a shift to corporate governance and leadership appointment\n\nCeleste, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s fastest growing lifestyle and quick commerce brands, has announced a landmark step in its evolution with the appointment of veteran corporate leader Roshanie J. Moraes and a strategic transition toward a strengthened corporate governance structure.\n\nSince its inception six years ago, Celeste has built a strong reputation through its commitment to quality, community and exceptional customer experience, offering round-the-clock convenience through its quick commerce partnerships with Uber Eats and PickMe Market.\n\nAs the brand continues to grow its presence both locally and globally, the move to a structured corporate model reflects Celeste\u2019s ambition to scale with discipline, strengthen its foundations and redefine what a modern Sri Lankan lifestyle and quick commerce brand can achieve. The move reflects Celeste\u2019s long-term vision of building a scalable, professionally governed institution capable of competing at both local and international levels.\n\n\u201cOver the past six years, Celeste has grown from a bold vision into a brand that truly resonates with Sri Lankans and this next step is a natural reflection of that journey. Bringing Roshanie onto our leadership team marks a defining moment for us and I am confident that her experience and vision will take Celeste to heights we have only just begun to imagine,\u201d said Celeste founder Janik Jayasuriya.\n\nRoshanie brings with her a distinguished career spanning nearly four decades in the Sri Lankan corporate sector. At JKH, she served in three of the key business sectors: transportation, retail and property development."
