    "description": "SL-Thailand Business Council celebrates 25 years of strengthening biz relations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/SL-Thailand-Business-Council-celebrates-25-years-of-strengthening-biz-relations/273-342671",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1781204771.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-06-12-dailymirrorlk-12809b59-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f6046c022f1a678fb03ea919ae191a5d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1619,
    "chunk_text": "SL-Thailand Business Council celebrates 25 years of strengthening biz relations\n\nSeated from left: Immediate Past President Dushyanta Basnayake, Counsellor Prangtip Kongridhisuksakorn, Past President Lalitha Kumarage, Vice President Kamil Weerasekara, Founder and Past President Lionel Fernando, Ambassador Paitoon Mahapannaporn, Founder and President Rizan Nazeer, Vice President A.M. Musajee, Treasurer Yashodha Peiris and Secretary Priyantha Kolonnage\n\nStanding from left: Committee Member Asitha Panabokka, Committee Member Chandana Nanayakkara, Assistant Secretary Rohan Elgiriyawithana, Committee Member Harendra Abeyesundere, Committee Member Rienzie Fernando, Assistant Treasurer Abdul Saliheen, Committee Member Aasim Mukthar and Committee Member Sanjeeva Jayasinghe\n\nThe Sri Lanka-Thailand Business Council (SLTBC) celebrates its 25th anniversary in 2026, marking a remarkable journey of fostering economic cooperation, trade, investment and friendship between Sri Lanka and Thailand.\n\nFor a quarter of a century, the SLTBC has served as a vital bridge connecting the private sectors of both nations, creating opportunities for businesses, facilitating dialogue and strengthening bilateral ties.\n\nEstablished at the dawn of a new millennium, the SLTBC emerged from a shared vision to promote closer commercial engagement between the two nations linked by centuries of cultural, religious and historical connections. Over the years, this vision has evolved into a dynamic platform that has supported entrepreneurs, investors, exporters and industry leaders in exploring new avenues of growth and collaboration."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
