    "chunk_size_bytes": 1843,
    "chunk_text": "Adamjee Lukmanjee Group  of Companies celebrates customers  at \u201cLegacy of Trust - Customer Forum 2026\u201d\n\nAdamjee Lukmanjee Group of Companies, a trusted name in Sri Lanka\u2019s agricultural and industrial supply sector with a proud legacy of 160 years, successfully hosted the \u201cLegacy of Trust - Customer Forum\u201926\u201d on 23 May 2026 at the Cinnamon Life, Colombo. The event was organised to appreciate and strengthen the long-standing relationships built with the company\u2019s valued customers and stakeholders over the years.\n\nWith a strong presence in the Sri Lankan market over the past 160 years, Adamjee Lukmanjee Group of Companies has continuously contributed to the country\u2019s agricultural, livestock and construction industries through its range of high-quality products including Animal Feed Ingredients, Saviya Cement and N-Joy Coconut Oil. The company has earned a reputation for reliability, consistency and customer-centric service, becoming a trusted partner for businesses across the island.\n\nThe event brought together customers, industry leaders, business partners and corporate representatives for a day of recognition, knowledge sharing and networking built on a foundation of trust. The forum highlighted the company\u2019s commitment to strengthening trust-driven, sustainable partnerships and creating long-term value for its customers. The keynote speakers for the event included renowned entrepreneur Araliya Group Chairman Dudley Sirisena, and economic policy analyst Dhananath Fernando from Advocata. Addressing the gathering, Dudley Sirisena shared valuable insights on entrepreneurship, resilience and the importance of empowering local industries. Dhananath Fernando spoke on the current economic landscape of Sri Lanka and the role of private sector collaboration in driving national growth and competitiveness."
